      "title": "Structure and components",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Evaluate candidate keys against distinct-value cardinality, value frequency and tenant skew, insert monotonicity, and common query shapes. High cardinality alone does not guarantee balanced load. Queries that omit the shard key or the prefix of a compound shard key require scatter-gather across the shards that may contain matching data. (high confidence) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/sharding-choose-a-shard-key.md ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/sharded-cluster-query-router.md",
