    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Choose the key and query shapes together. Queries that include the shard key or a prefix of it can be targeted to a subset of shards, while queries without the shard key are broadcast to all shards. If the data has high-frequency values, a compound key that adds a unique or low-frequency field can help; with a tenant-first prefix, queries filtering on tenant can be targeted. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/sharding-choose-a-shard-key/ ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/sharded-cluster-query-router/",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/sharding-choose-a-shard-key/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ba6c285abdab691bcedbb09fa5ffd8595ddc60317ee3b285bc96d3d38b94bbbe",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
