          }
        },
        {
          "text": "For a shared-collection multi-tenant design, store tenantId on every document and include it in every query. When tenant-scoped reads and writes dominate, including tenantId in the shard key aligns routing with the application’s tenant boundary; the boundary remains logical and must be enforced in application code. (medium confidence) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/build-multi-tenant-arch.md ; https://mongodb.com/docs/vector-search/deployment/multi-tenant-architecture/ ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/sharded-cluster-query-router.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/build-multi-tenant-arch.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:52552bb94cdbc79f94d93af4a29878526f6caaed771e7a4dc24a2b8ebfe3dbb4",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
