    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "With a range shard key consisting only of tenantId, all documents for a tenant share one shard-key value. Each unique shard key value can exist on no more than a single chunk at any given time, so a very large or active tenant cannot be split by tenantId alone and its chunk can become an indivisible bottleneck on one shard. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/sharding-choose-a-shard-key/",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/sharding-choose-a-shard-key/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:13eaf9c55ae56b76f165414afc12f5ff1715cf1218de824e8a22b51bf866f070",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
