            "claim_text_sha256": "5fbd238dd55e40191aa593d64c5cf8129063b122396f6de8a759fc71062b2ed6"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "For insert-heavy workloads with monotonic suffix values, a compound hashed key such as {tenantId: 1, _id: \"hashed\"} can distribute inserts more evenly within the tenant-prefixed key space. Hashed shard keys trade range locality on the hashed field for more even distribution; MongoDB supports one hashed field in a compound hashed key. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-19)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/hashed-sharding/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5c046777bf065e636b1058558d33c65d772de25d90340dd92c861263850cce63",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2df53a55b4d68cc553ab6bebda34fc5ed17cae6cbea74f2938acd3edd0150919",
            "ev:d00f33f9820ccc7ef80d8ccf52e5da9b8a0f7818ddd762a079d5d17d1e86cc96",
            "ev:e03a4ee34d0162eaa0c7b73814877125ea1eb421ad4bf025d59607e36d087989"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/yorkie-team/yorkie/blob/main/docs/design/mongodb-sharding.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In shared collections, tenantId is logical segmentation: queries must filter by tenantId and the application tier must enforce tenant access controls. MongoDB's Vector Search guidance also uses tenant_id as a prefilter for tenant-scoped searches. (high confidence) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/build-multi-tenant-arch.md ; https://mongodb.com/docs/vector-search/deployment/multi-tenant-architecture/",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/build-multi-tenant-arch.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:52ede5823c34dffb87f0b42ab772b3d9f153c3cfa0445fccac339bfbe5c10063",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
